  "annotated_box": "box_w, box_h, size_px, off and the scale s always describe the annotated box, also for view-cut samples",
  "partial_objects": "vis < 1. View-cut objects: the window is centred on the visible part of the box; vis_w, vis_h (source px) and vis_off (window px, equal to the jitter) describe that part, off locates the centre of the annotated box and is therefore not (0,0) for a centred cut window. Frame-edge objects are annotated clipped, so their box_w, box_h, size_px are those of the clipped box and vis_w, vis_h repeat them",
  "negatives": "label 16, track \"background\". size_px, box_w, box_h are those of the matched positive (they fixed level and scale), vis is 1.0",
  "extra_arrays": [
